WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:05.600
There's a church in the city of Bethlehem.

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:10.100
It was built on the spot where Christians believe Jesus was born.

00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:13.340
It's called the Church of the Nativity.

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:17.820
If you consult UNESCO's List of World Heritage Sites,

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:20.700
or ask travel expert Rick Steves,

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:23.940
both will tell you that the church is in Palestine.

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:27.620
But when a question about the church's location came up

00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:30.580
during a round
of Jeopardy in January 2020...

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:35.380
What is Palestine?

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:35.880
No.

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:36.380
What is Israel?

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:37.060
That's it.

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:41.420
That answer set off something
of an internet firestorm.

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:51.940
That's because what you call this land,
and who controls it, is at the center of

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:55.940
a decades-long conflict between Israelis
and Palestinians.

00:00:56.440 --> 00:00:59.640
But more recently, there is also a third group

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:04.300
that is becoming more and more influential here and throughout the Middle East,

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:07.640
American evangelical Christians.

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:11.360
Today, evangelical Christians are one of the most

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:14.420
politically powerful voting blocs in the United States.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:19.240
And in the Trump administration, they've been given unprecedented power.

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:23.420
They've turned support for Israel and hostility towards its enemies

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:26.660
into core tenets of conservative ideology.

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:30.240
And a big part of those policies is rooted

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:32.040
in how they interpret the Bible.

00:01:36.740 --> 00:01:40.280
In 2016, more than a quarter of all US voters

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:43.060
identified as white evangelical Christians.

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:49.200
One of the primary differences between evangelicals
and other Christians is their

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:50.820
relationship with the Bible.

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:54.560
Conservative evangelicals believe that the Bible is literally true.

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:58.800
Sarah Posner writes about religion for a bunch of different publications.

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:02.770
Many of them believe that the Bible is sort of this prophetic

00:02:02.770 --> 00:02:08.920
road map for modern life, that events
described and prophesied in the Bible

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:10.340
will it will become true.

00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:13.400
The Bible is the most historically accurate book ever penned.

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:19.480
The Bible is the one book that
dares to predict the future with 100% accuracy.

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:23.560
For evangelicals, the most
important of the Bible's prophecies is

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:26.920
the second coming, when Jesus will return
to Earth.

00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:29.460
The Bible doesn't say when this will happen,

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:31.440
but it does say where.

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:32.820
This is Jerusalem.

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:36.820
World history as we know it is going to
end right here.

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:39.780
Greg Laurie is an evangelical preacher,

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:43.299
one of several who
meet regularly to advise President Trump.

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:47.660
They're the leaders of megachurches
with tens of thousands of members.

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:53.180
And many of them, including Greg Laurie,
preach a belief called Christian Zionism,

00:02:53.180 --> 00:02:58.040
the idea that the return of the Jewish
people to Israel is one of a series of

00:02:58.040 --> 00:03:01.200
events that will trigger Jesus's second
coming.

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:06.440
Jesus is telling us that the rebirth of Israel is a sign of the end.

00:03:06.440 --> 00:03:09.520
Not just a sign, it's the super sign.

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:13.920
According to this theology, God will
reward those who help Israel

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:15.840
and punish those who don't.

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:19.230
Jesus will be on his
throne and he separates the nations.

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:22.800
On what basis? How they treated Zion.

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:24.800
Let's back up.

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:29.620
After the Holocaust, the UN divided up the then-British territory of Palestine,

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:32.560
home to more than a million Arabs, into two states,

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:35.700
giving Jews who had been persecuted in Europe a homeland.

00:03:36.340 --> 00:03:40.620
Over the next few decades, Israel fought
multiple wars with its Arab neighbors

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:45.320
and seized much of the land that had
been originally set aside for Palestinians.

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:49.820
Evangelical Christians see that as a fulfillment of Biblical prophecy.

00:03:49.820 --> 00:03:54.380
It happened exactly as foretold. It was a miraculous act of God.

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:57.640
They own that land, and they own that city.

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:02.920
Ever since, groups like Hamas have been
fighting against the Israelis trying to

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:04.460
win that territory back.

00:04:04.460 --> 00:04:08.920
And the government of Iran has been one of their biggest supporters.

00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:23.960
That's part of the reason Iran plays
such an important role in evangelical beliefs

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:26.940
about the present state of the
world, and the future.

00:04:27.540 --> 00:04:29.560
According to Christian Zionism,

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:33.320
if the US wants to be
on the right side of biblical prophecy,

00:04:33.320 --> 00:04:38.220
they need to do everything possible to
protect Israel and punish Iran.

00:04:39.380 --> 00:04:44.240
That also helps explain why a different Bible story is also really important to them.

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:49.030
The Old Testament story of Esther, about
a plot to destroy the Jews of Persia,

00:04:49.030 --> 00:04:50.760
or modern-day Iran.

00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:54.320
The Book of Esther plays
such an important role for Christian Zionists

00:04:54.320 --> 00:04:56.400
they've made multiple movies out of it.

00:04:56.400 --> 00:05:00.400
He has convinced your husband to destroy all the Jews, including you.

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:03.820
Esther saves the Jews by using her persuasion with the king.

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:07.080
Evangelicals who are very
wrapped up in this kind of theology,

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:13.440
because Persia is modern-day Iran, they
sort of contextualize this Bible story

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:15.540
into foreign policies.

00:05:16.820 --> 00:05:21.400
Could it be that that President Trump right now has been sort of raised for such a time as this,

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:25.480
just like Queen Esther. to help save the Jewish people from an Iranian Menace?

00:05:25.480 --> 00:05:28.140
As a Christian I certainly believe that's possible.

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:30.100
I'm confident that the Lord is
at work here.

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:36.160
Secretary of state Mike Pompeo and vice president Mike Pence both identify as evangelical Christians.

00:05:36.760 --> 00:05:40.340
And both have enormous influence over
American foreign policy.

00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:45.560
A ProPublica investigation found that Pence routed
millions of dollars in foreign aid

00:05:45.560 --> 00:05:49.540
that had been earmarked for humanitarian projects in Iraq, diverting it towards

00:05:49.540 --> 00:05:51.120
Christian groups in the country.

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:58.180
When President Trump approved the drone strike that killed Iran's top military commander in January 2020,

00:05:58.180 --> 00:06:02.840
it was, according to the Washington Post, at Pompeo and Pence's urging.

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:08.300
When President Trump moved the US Embassy in Israel from Tel Aviv to Jerusalem,

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:12.960
the move had more support from American evangelicals
than American Jews.

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:18.680
The other news swirling around the embassy's move to
Jerusalem is what it could signal as part of biblical prophecy.

00:06:18.680 --> 00:06:20.980
Donald Trump recognized history.

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:23.260
He, like King Cyrus before him,

00:06:23.260 --> 00:06:26.060
fulfilled the biblical prophecy.

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:29.180
That evangelical support isn't an accident.

00:06:29.180 --> 00:06:30.880
The Trump administration courts it.

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:35.160
After the administration put out a peace plan that would have given Israel

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:38.000
unprecedented control over Palestinian land,

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:41.920
The Christian broadcast network interviewed Trump's ambassador to Israel.

00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:45.320
You're talking about opening up the Bible, bringing it back to life in ways

00:06:45.320 --> 00:06:49.280
that I think your listeners could
not have even have imagined.

00:06:49.280 --> 00:06:56.040
it's an opportunity for biblical tourism that I think will grow and flourish in profound ways.

00:06:56.040 --> 00:06:58.340
The network's coverage
followed his lead.

00:06:58.340 --> 00:07:00.420
Good news in this proposed peace plan.

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:04.560
Israel would have sovereignty over many historical biblical sites.

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:11.060
For evangelical Christians in America, the Bible isn't just a foundational text,

00:07:11.060 --> 00:07:15.700
it's a prophetic road map that tells the future and shapes the way they view the present.

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:21.360
And for an influential group of them, that motivates their support for a foreign policy

00:07:21.360 --> 00:07:24.480
that they see as affirming those prophecies,

00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:28.200
and a president who depends on their
votes.

00:07:39.800 --> 00:07:41.860
you

